\par\medskip
The curvature R of a \(
atural -biextension\) P is the curvature of the connection on P. It is a translation-invariant 2-form on \(G_{1}	imes G_{2}\) with values in Lie(H), i.e. an alternating form on \(\operatorname{Lie}(G_{1})	imes \operatorname{Lie}(G_{2})\) with values in Lie(H). Its restriction to \(\operatorname{Lie}(G_{1})\) and to \(\operatorname{Lie}(G_{2})\) is zero, so that R defines a pairing (also called the curvature of P)\par
